<!-- FOUNDER -->
<section id="founder" style="border-top:1px solid var(--border);">
  <div style="max-width:680px;">
    <div class="section-label">The Founder</div>
    <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Tristan Stuetzel.</h2>
    <div style="font-size:0.72rem;color:var(--muted);letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:2.5rem;">Founder & Director · Chico State, Class of '29 · First-Generation College Student</div>
    <div style="font-size:1rem;line-height:1.95;color:var(--muted);">
      <p>At 5 years old, I was taken by social services. My little brother was 1. We bounced from placement to placement — two kids with no certainty of where we'd end up, growing up in motels, not knowing what came next.</p><br/>
      <p>We got lucky. A family took us both in and gave us opportunities we couldn't have imagined. I can't give them enough credit. They changed our trajectory completely.</p><br/>
      <p>But we have another little brother who didn't come with us. He's still out there — one of the kids the system leaves behind. <span style="color:var(--white);">He's the reason Adoptare exists.</span></p><br/>
      <p>From a young age I was told I was different — that I wouldn't graduate high school, that I'd end up a statistic. I refused to believe it. I broke the cycle. I'm now a 19-year-old first-generation college student at Chico State, and everything I do is to prove to my brothers that we are not defined by what happened to us.</p><br/>
      <p style="color:var(--white);font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:500;border-left:2px solid var(--accent);padding-left:1.25rem;line-height:1.7;">"We are not doomed by our story. It's our origin that defines us — and every foster kid and adoptee should be proud enough to wear it."</p>
      <br/>
      <p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:0.85rem;font-style:italic;border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding-top:1.5rem;">This is for my little brother David — we were told we'd never amount to anything. I need you to know that nothing we went through changes what we are capable of. Don't give up. This one's for you.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- MISSION -->
<section id="mission">
